From, 2026-10-03. Apply in vendor/decomp-permuter (upstream 059609d):
    git apply ../../canon-tools/patches/decomp-permuter-deref-function.patch
Why: this decomp writes every call the game makes through a register as "(*func_X)(args)"
(IDO compiles it to a jalr; "func_X(args)" is a jal), and the permuter's type pass crashed on
it ("dereferencing non-pointer", beffect.c func_80198750 at iteration 3). "*f" of a function
designator is the function itself (C11 6.5.3.2).

diff --git a/src/ast_types.py b/src/ast_types.py
index 50e6b89..b34ffc8 100644
--- a/src/ast_types.py
+++ b/src/ast_types.py
@@ -75,6 +75,9 @@ def get_decl_type(decl: ca.Decl) -> Type:

 def deref_type(type: Type, typemap: TypeMap) -> Type:
     type = resolve_typedefs(type, typemap)
+    if isinstance(type, ca.FuncDecl):
+        # "*f" of a function designator is the function itself (C11 6.5.3.2), as in "(*f)()"
+        return type
     assert isinstance(type, (ca.ArrayDecl, ca.PtrDecl)), "dereferencing non-pointer"
     return type.type

